#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481728} :activity/id #uuid "0fc222ec-8ee3-576a-8975-559e2c61b885" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051085 :topic/id #uuid "7fdf89be-7454-5a23-9d34-17c62e869eea" :topic/math-academy-id 2132} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481700 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77742b04-e958-51e3-885d-c186ce960ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437856} {:answer/id #uuid "7a46d360-0b63-59bd-8d4c-b0aa9e72d4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437857}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437856} :answer-field/id #uuid "24781376-5a9f-5184-b064-24b3c476bb79" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438957} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d33cbee7-fc8b-5c3d-bfba-41b228bb82bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437858} {:answer/id #uuid "923f7469-7fef-5157-a155-0ff72c5145be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437859}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437859} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfb64428-9f16-5737-8c74-c42a032a0297" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438958} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058fa0b3-ef79-5a7a-afc6-113a760e3e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437860} {:answer/id #uuid "5292bd0e-9d53-564c-bffc-65c61607f30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437861}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437861} :answer-field/id #uuid "52c67e92-c96c-5d8b-b9f6-cc9263317637" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438959} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6613a08-4056-5a9f-9ca6-c3c5e4078896" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437862} {:answer/id #uuid "e701c30a-31e0-5846-a5ac-4931665193d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437863}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437862} :answer-field/id #uuid "387cbfbf-b068-513c-93c4-71cb2f6085f2" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1a88235e-0bbc-5c38-af1d-92f6a6eda26f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131361" :question/problem "![](images/17/1709a94b7361a1e8764d94199f9e84802ae925a09e6481250d0846b83bb6549f.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction.\n- **IV.** $F$ is irrotational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/7c/7c831425eae7afd709d546a8e05100f495adc04bba6450cfa56d370b415a28f5.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate clockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (clockwise), our thumb will point into the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points into from the screen, in the direction of decreasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "5cb2647d-9528-5c30-ba8e-54caf973f4e8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481740}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481728 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c74d4b9-7ed4-529a-b818-13e80317f0ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446560} {:answer/id #uuid "976ecb2e-4f04-5610-8207-c96b23772842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446561} {:answer/id #uuid "b06370cf-7aa1-54f8-9e46-dc3a42a8d19d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446563} {:answer/id #uuid "c7df0803-65d5-5e82-a045-a191ec18b671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446564} {:answer/id #uuid "e214b4cf-1c30-5601-8ce0-ad80b4de52ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446567}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446560} :answer-field/id #uuid "b667cd59-08f8-5c6e-82c5-8b3ea70d6405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "40fa6adc-4679-5e13-a9fc-cb698f54e0e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105700" :question/problem "![](images/18/183ea541b33b8389de46f9ee1560ed1da2b999191477d7490eb4970922bdc43c.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n\nII. $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $F$ is not irrotational\n\nIV. $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/b1/b1520791fcb3808604758b7d8f99443020d12075d4cc8bff78659880575b6ef2.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements III and IV are false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational. And, since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :step/id #uuid "ad78c5c9-ad7f-533a-a2ae-0ae1700b578f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481749}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481731 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262630 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "221ac97f-6559-509a-a3d9-2450bf49633e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260172} {:answer/id #uuid "a2757385-050d-54a8-8369-31a9aa26112c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261289} {:answer/id #uuid "b7289054-f9d1-5ae6-bd2a-f55dcf3e02b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261483} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb179e1-20cb-58d0-b8da-a19ff4125371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262076} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd94cc3-eb96-53bb-8a15-64be7834efb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262088}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262076} :answer-field/id #uuid "8edf0788-7859-57f4-ac13-2b85b5bf5d5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4b1f3451-5b4c-525b-84a2-e17f8516fc90" :question/math-academy-id "q-126547" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\,i+({x}^{2}-y)\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =2x-2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c486f1f0-e8fa-5c16-9036-44a2ad1aee07" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481700}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481740 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446572 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f352f1a-1af2-5144-a245-10854ead8b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446554} {:answer/id #uuid "41e8b7d6-5c7a-5cf8-9c06-4d00a18513e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446557} {:answer/id #uuid "834c390d-d089-5913-89c4-08a44764f21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446558} {:answer/id #uuid "dcefe323-f572-5c28-853b-0586c0615884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446565} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c44a28-6809-582c-b411-ffd64f99822a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446568}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446565} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfc4e87e-69ab-505e-8ac2-a813c8707da5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "322bc9a1-81a0-53ce-920d-1108825e3484" :question/math-academy-id "q-131363" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5ac051f640c2b4eae760eee9c567ec35ce3169384ec2305554e21c6d2d587bbe.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n\nII. $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction.\n\nIV. $F$ is irrotational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/80/80c67e624f960147b7980ee90700be800a414ab1e2a2e47faf7e8821ee0c0623.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "dda57262-1ccc-5da1-bbd4-59647bd6412a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481749 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d194d4-bd3d-507f-8c59-044dbc7c81ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446555} {:answer/id #uuid "2afb3ad3-3542-5efb-92a8-0a844c4e01a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446556} {:answer/id #uuid "8854556c-9dbd-5890-ab92-8f478346b8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446559} {:answer/id #uuid "98578e86-a0e6-513f-9db5-c6b91293012b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446562} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f07f8f-3a33-5658-92ff-2b538d7dcca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446566}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446555} :answer-field/id #uuid "9999ac46-6f4e-593f-907b-51eaf6bed9c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aedf76f0-5451-58bc-9366-057502daac94" :question/math-academy-id "q-126522" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=(3x+2y)\\,i+({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x+2y) \\\\  & =-2x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(-2,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(-2,1)} & =-2(-2)-2 \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f9980b60-ddef-518f-9c60-dd36d6feb6c5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481731}}] :activity/title "The Curl of a Vector Field" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481564}]}
